  "title": "BIS Raises Gold and Silver Hallmarking Fees Amid Concerns",
  "summary": "The Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) has raised gold and silver hallmarking fees to ₹75 from ₹45 and ₹35 respectively, with immediate effect ahead of the festive season. The revised regulations aim to address concerns about fake hallmarking and unauthorised operators, while maintaining a minimum charge structure.",
